1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:00,909
Picture this.

2
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:04,141
You're in front of the whole class, your slides are on the projector,

3
00:00:04,191 --> 00:00:07,000
and for every new slide you have to walk back to your laptop.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,882
Or you ask a friend to click for you,

5
00:00:09,932 --> 00:00:12,179
and somehow they're always one slide behind.

6
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,521
That's why I built SlimClick.

7
00:00:14,571 --> 00:00:16,743
It turns your phone into a presentation remote,

8
00:00:16,793 --> 00:00:18,730
and you don't even have to install an app.

9
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:23,988
You open SlimClick on your laptop, scan the QR code with your phone's camera,

10
00:00:24,038 --> 00:00:25,144
and a web page opens.

11
00:00:25,194 --> 00:00:26,189
That's your remote.

12
00:00:27,199 --> 00:00:28,545
Now you just tap next.

13
00:00:28,595 --> 00:00:32,539
It works with PowerPoint, Keynote, Google Slides and even PDFs.

14
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,631
Your phone also shows a live preview of the current slide,

15
00:00:36,681 --> 00:00:39,960
so you can face your audience and still know exactly where you are.

16
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:42,359
Want to point at something?

17
00:00:42,409 --> 00:00:44,346
Turn on the laser, touch the preview,

18
00:00:44,396 --> 00:00:47,139
and a red dot appears right there on the big screen.

19
00:00:47,189 --> 00:00:49,180
The spotlight darkens everything else.

20
00:00:50,179 --> 00:00:51,411
There's a timer as well.

21
00:00:51,461 --> 00:00:54,828
A few minutes before the end, your phone screen flashes quietly,

22
00:00:54,878 --> 00:00:56,590
so you never run over time again.

23
00:00:57,589 --> 00:00:59,701
And if your school Wi-Fi blocks the connection,

24
00:00:59,751 --> 00:01:03,059
SlimClick shows you step by step how to use your phone's hotspot instead.

25
00:01:04,790 --> 00:01:05,668
It's also secure.

26
00:01:05,718 --> 00:01:08,564
The QR code only works once, every command is signed,

27
00:01:08,614 --> 00:01:12,170
and nobody else can take over your slides without your permission.

28
00:01:13,170 --> 00:01:17,475
SlimClick is completely free for Windows and Mac, with no ads and no account.

29
00:01:17,525 --> 00:01:19,737
You'll find the link in the description.

30
00:01:19,787 --> 00:01:21,886
Good luck with your next presentation.
